<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tzanetos Grigorakis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zanetbey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tzanetos Grigorakis, known as Zanetbey, was bey of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mani">Mani</a> in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> from 1782 to 1798, under Ottoman overlordship. From the Grigorakis clan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gytheio">Gytheio</a> area, he governed the feuding Maniot chieftain families and paid the tribute owed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. He kept contacts with Christian powers hostile to the Ottomans, was deposed in 1798, and continued to resist from his tower strongholds.</p></div>
